# microtapes.txt -- the tapes on the Type 550 Microtape drives. Copy this file to
# /opt/pidp1-mods/microtapes.txt and edit it.
# See Docs/UsingType550Microtape.md.
#
# One line per drive:  <drive> <image>[,locked]
#   drive    1-8, in decimal (drive 8 is 10 in the mse unit field)
#   image    the tape image file. A path that does not start with / is relative to
#            /opt/pidp1-mods/Microtapes.
#            It runs to the end of the line and may contain spaces.
#   ,locked  the WRITE LOCK switch: the drive can be read but not written or erased.
#            A read-only image file is always mounted locked.
#
# A missing image is created as a blank tape unless the line is locked.
# Tts directory must already exist, /opt/pidp1-mods/Microtapes will already be created.
# A drive with no # line has no tape, mlc on it gives tape unable.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# After editing, a SIGHUP to pidp1 remounts the drives whose lines
# changed, any drive whose tape ran off its reel, and any drive whose line failed to mount last
# time.
# The others are unchanged, including tapes a program mounted with the IOT mmt, 720201.
#
# The sequence break channel is set by microtapesbs in pidp1.config.

#1 scratch.tap
#2 zgame.tap
